[size=5][b]Description[/b][/size]
Skhroma brings Razer Chroma lighting to Skyrim. It is an SKSE plugin that turns every Chroma device you own (keyboard, mouse, mousepad, keypad, headset and Chroma Link) into an extension of the HUD and the world around you.

Your health, magicka and stamina live on your keyboard. The room glows with torchlight when you step indoors, snow drifts across the keys in a blizzard, embers creep in from the edges when a fight starts, and your whole desk pulses with a heartbeat when you are close to death.

It is pure SKSE: no .esp, no scripts, no plugin slot, no save bloat. You can add or remove it at any time, even mid-playthrough.

[size=5][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install the requirements below.
[*]Install Skhroma with Mod Organizer 2 or Vortex. For a manual install, extract the archive into your Skyrim Data folder.
[*]Make sure Razer Synapse is running with Chroma enabled before you launch the game.
[*](Optional) Edit [b]SKSE/Plugins/Skhroma.ini[/b] to taste.
[/list]
The archive contains only:
[code]SKSE/Plugins/Skhroma.dll
SKSE/Plugins/Skhroma.ini
SKSE/Plugins/Skhroma.pdb[/code]
The .pdb is optional. It only helps crash loggers name Skhroma functions if something goes wrong.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] disable or delete the mod. Nothing is stored in your save.

[b]Troubleshooting[/b]
[list]
[*]Log: Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/Skhroma.log
[*]No lights? Check that Synapse is running and that the log says "Chroma SDK initialized".
[*]Lights flickering between effects? Another app is also driving Chroma. Close it or turn off its Chroma integration while playing.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[b]Keyboard[/b]
[list]
[*]F1-F4 Magicka, F5-F8 Health, F9-F12 Stamina: live bars that drain and refill
[*]Movement keys (WASD by default) light up in combat and fade when you run low on stamina
[*]Shout key (Z by default): dim while recovering, gold when ready
[*]Movement and shout keys follow your in-game key bindings
[*]Numpad: SunHelm hunger, thirst, fatigue and cold meters
[*]ESC blinks red as an alarm when health is low or a SunHelm need becomes critical
[/list]
[b]Mouse:[/b] left strip shows Health, right strip shows Stamina.
[b]Mousepad:[/b] the ring mirrors the HUD (Magicka / Health / Stamina).
[b]Keypad:[/b] the four SunHelm meters plus a Health column.
[b]Headset and Chroma Link:[/b] ambient color and every global effect.

[b]World and events (on every device)[/b]
[list]
[*]Time of day: dawn, daylight, dusk and night colors outdoors; warm torchlight indoors
[*]Weather: clouds, rain drops, snow flakes and lightning flashes in thunderstorms
[*]Combat embers, sneaking, swimming
[*]Werewolf, Vampire Lord and vampire tints
[*]Low-health heartbeat, red flash when hit, blue-white flash when blocking
[*]Level-up wave and dragon soul absorption
[*]Bleedout and death
[*]SunHelm cold: frost creeps in from the edges as you freeze
[*]Menus dim the lights, with special looks for the map, lockpicking and sleep/wait
[/list]

[b]Fully configurable[/b]
Every device and every effect can be switched on or off in Skhroma.ini. You can also tune overall and ambient brightness, frame rate, what counts as "low" health / magicka / stamina, and the Health, Magicka, Stamina, Frost and Combat colors.

[b]Lightweight[/b]
Game state is sampled about 15 times per second on the main thread, and lighting runs on its own thread at 30 fps. The game never waits on Chroma.

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url]
[*]Razer Synapse with Chroma enabled, or any other RzChromaSDK64.dll provider (for example open-chroma)
[*]At least one Razer Chroma device
[/list]
[b]Optional[/b]
[list]
[*][b]SunHelm Survival:[/b] enables the hunger, thirst, fatigue and cold meters and the frost effect. Skhroma detects it automatically. Without it these layers simply stay off.
[*][b]Dawnguard[/b] (included in every SE/AE copy): enables the Vampire Lord look.
[/list]
[b]Compatibility[/b]
[list]
[*]Skyrim SE 1.5.97 and AE 1.6.x (version independent through Address Library). Tested on Nolvus Awakening 6 (1.5.97). Not compatible with Skyrim VR.
[*]Compatible with everything. It does not touch any records, meshes or scripts.
[/list]

